  {
   "text": "Figure 5. United States data. (a) Of 207,508 agency fire records (2018 to 2020) that no standard satellite product labelled,\n4,343 are verified (blue; whisker: 95% interval, 2.03–2.16%), 20,913 probable (hatched) and 182,252 record-only (white). (b)\nFor 45 of 240 fires (2023–2025) the first label moved earlier; median lead 42 min (bootstrap 95%: 22–84 min; square with\nwhiskers), each circle one fire. (c) One record's patches (␣×k = k trailing spaces); boxed cells changed. The national run\ncleaned 2.66 million records in 7.9 minutes. Source: wildfireguardiandata results/HEADLINE_NUMBERS.md and release v0.1.",
